type look
version 1
---
# The game's look (og-taste §12): the frame's art direction as data, named
# by GameDesc.look in src/main.ts and applied before start runs. It starts
# from the catalogue's 16bit-pixel preset (a 224-pixel-tall frame, eight-tone
# ramps, a Bayer dither: the camera's 14 units are 16 pixels each, one per
# texel of the tiles); a block written below wins over the preset field by
# field, and `extends` takes any catalogue slug. `npm create @origingame/game`
# writes the game's own look from its premise, or from --look <slug>.
name "Origin Game 2D"
extends "16bit-pixel"
